    "body": "Reviewer: Codex CLI 0.157.1, gpt-6-astra, medium effort. Head 7786728.\n\nThe REST checks confirm the listed PR branches and review states, all six claimed merges including #112, the listed issue open/closed states, and both active rulesets; no merged or closed PR is called open. Two operator instructions are missing or superseded in ways that would make the incoming coordinator resume the wrong workflow. There are no previous reviews or threads on #119 to resolve.\n\nFindings:\n\n- Blocking P2 — Replace the superseded 14-minute heartbeat recovery instructions with the current Monitor/digest, merge-train, and hourly fallback procedure; see the inline finding at line 61.\n- Blocking P2 — Preserve the operator's explicit coordinator-only delegation rule, including issue/brief authoring and routine investigation; see the inline finding at line 43.\n\nNon-blocking snapshot drift: REST now reports seven open PRs including this PR and 55 open issues including #117 and #118, both created after the recorded snapshot. These additions do not invalidate the timestamped count; include the wake/channel issues when updating the affected recovery instructions.\n\nValidation: read issue #114, the project plan, the full one-page diff, PR comments/reviews, coordinator raw notes, the named scripts, and local worktree paths. All named files exist, the holding directory is mode 700 and ignored, and manual inspection found no secret or token value in the page. `mise run check:handoff` exited 0 but reported no recognized open-PR references, so the table was verified independently through REST rather than relying on that classifier. The reviewed head's docs, pr-body, imported-research, and mutation checks passed; check was still running at the API read. No aggregate or formatter was run in this read-only checkout, and no repository files were changed.",
