    "body": "Reviewer: Codex CLI 0.157.1, gpt-6-astra, medium effort. Head 13c9bc1.\n\nReviewed against issue #114 and the coordinator's 2026-09-26 scope exception: both published archives preserve the actual startup files byte for byte after frontmatter and provenance notes, and the prompt page identifies the incoming session that used it. The earlier wake-procedure and coordinator-delegation findings are fixed in the named commits and preserved in the archived prompt; both threads are now resolved. The timestamped roster is historical under the coordinator's direction, so subsequent state changes do not require rewriting it.\n\nFindings:\n- Blocking: none.\n- Non-blocking: none remaining.\n\nValidation: read AGENTS.md, the project plan, issue #114, all PR comments/reviews and thread replies, the main-to-head diff, and the named fixing commits. Independently compared both archives with the main checkout's .holding/handoff sources: 25,906 and 7,138 bytes, with SHA-256 values matching the committed evidence report. A redacted gitleaks scan of those source files exited 0 with no leaks; manual inspection of the changes found no secret values, and no redactions were needed. git diff --check passed. All five required CI checks succeeded at this head. This changes documentation and prose exemptions only, so no core/shell behavior or runtime tests change. I did not rerun aggregate checks, builds, or formatters in the read-only checkout; no repository files were changed.",
